From 9508bc741512c2e725d7b25b9a1c7225ce0e9f39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:57:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] async_delegation: wake the parent chat for a result
 no live poller delivers

A pending terminal async-delegation result now reaches its parent chat without
anyone reopening it. tui_gateway/delegation_unloaded.py runs from the kanban
unloaded-session sweeper loop in every Desktop/TUI backend: a UI-dispatched
result past a 90 s grace, not under a live delivery claim, is claimed in the
ledger (the one cross-process gate) and run as one turn in the parent via
server._wake_session_turn (resumed here when no backend holds it). Started =
ack; busy/refused/error = defer with backoff; per-chat wake budget.

Covers the three gaps behind deleg_5facc89f's 8 h lag (2026-11-11): parent
loaded nowhere; parent loaded headless (startup_replay copies need a live
transport); parent held by backend B while backend A's SESSION_NOT_OWNED
retries keep the row 'recently touched', so B's orphan sweep never re-offers
it (reproduced in test_tail_repro_...).
